WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:02.133
-How does that feel?
-Amazing.

00:00:02.133 --> 00:00:04.067
-I mean, people, we're back.
-People!

00:00:04.067 --> 00:00:05.834
-The people are here --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:05.834 --> 00:00:08.501
-Uma Thurman is
on "The Tonight Show." Come on.

00:00:08.501 --> 00:00:10.667
You look fantastic.
-Oh, my God. Thank you.

00:00:10.667 --> 00:00:14.634
This is my first time in front
of a live audience

00:00:14.634 --> 00:00:17.701
in a long time.
-It feels good, right?

00:00:17.701 --> 00:00:19.200
-It really does.
-You look fantastic.

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:22.434
How are you? How is the family?
-The family is good.

00:00:22.434 --> 00:00:24.968
-Good. Knock on wood, yeah.
How about Maya?

00:00:24.968 --> 00:00:27.667
-Maya is great.
-Crushing.

00:00:27.667 --> 00:00:31.033
She's following in the footsteps
of her mom, she's an actress --

00:00:31.033 --> 00:00:32.467
-Both her parents.
-Both her parents as well.

00:00:32.467 --> 00:00:33.767
-Actually, I wouldn't say
she's following our footsteps.

00:00:33.767 --> 00:00:35.667
She's crushing it.
-She's crushing it

00:00:35.667 --> 00:00:37.968
on "Stranger Things."
-Yeah, doing great.

00:00:37.968 --> 00:00:41.667
-I remember I was hanging out
with you, and Maya --

00:00:41.667 --> 00:00:43.634
-She was this big.
-Yeah, she was a baby,

00:00:43.634 --> 00:00:45.767
and you were reading her
"Ferdinand."

00:00:45.767 --> 00:00:47.367
-"Ferdinand," I know.
-That was the book you were

00:00:47.367 --> 00:00:49.567
reading and I was like --
I didn't know what that was

00:00:49.567 --> 00:00:52.501
at the time.
So, and I remember --

00:00:52.501 --> 00:00:54.234
-Now you do.
-I have two little girls.

00:00:54.234 --> 00:00:55.501
And I read them "Ferdinand."

00:00:55.501 --> 00:00:57.901
So, you have a small part
in raising my children.

00:00:57.901 --> 00:00:59.934
-I like that. I like that.
-You did a great job.

00:00:59.934 --> 00:01:03.300
-"Ferdinand," you know,
the bull that won't fight.

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:05.400
-I love it, it's the greatest.
The greatest book.

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:07.734
She's keep crushing it.
Did you know "Stranger Things"

00:01:07.734 --> 00:01:09.067
before she was on it?
-Oh, yeah.

00:01:09.067 --> 00:01:11.634
Her brother and I watched the
whole thing. We loved it.

00:01:11.634 --> 00:01:14.801
She actually didn't even know
about it when she auditioned.

00:01:14.801 --> 00:01:16.100
-She didn't know about it
and you knew about it.

00:01:16.100 --> 00:01:17.501
You're like,
"Oh, no. We know --"

00:01:17.501 --> 00:01:19.567
-No, because he was like my TV
watching partner.

00:01:19.567 --> 00:01:22.400
And we're like, "Okay, this
whole thing's TV revolution

00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:24.133
that's going on.
I've got to figure it out."

00:01:24.133 --> 00:01:26.901
-Yeah.
-So, my son and I watched it.

00:01:26.901 --> 00:01:28.234
-Binge watched everything.
-Yeah.

00:01:28.234 --> 00:01:30.000
We would watch altogether.
-And does she let you know

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:33.267
any spoilers or anything or --
-No, no.

00:01:33.267 --> 00:01:34.467
-She's good.
-She's good.

00:01:34.467 --> 00:01:36.033
-Good kid, yeah.
-She's good, yeah. She's solid.

00:01:36.033 --> 00:01:39.000
-Does she ask for advice?
-Only occasionally.

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:40.133
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:01:40.133 --> 00:01:41.734
She knows everything,
like all children.

00:01:41.734 --> 00:01:43.667
-Like all children do, yeah.
She's crushing it.

00:01:43.667 --> 00:01:45.200
Tell her congratulations.
-I will.

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:47.434
She wants to come on your show.
-She -- oh, my gosh.

00:01:47.434 --> 00:01:49.067
Maya, come on the show.
We'll talk about --

00:01:49.067 --> 00:01:54.367
[ Cheers and applause ]
We'll read "Ferdinand."

00:01:54.367 --> 00:01:55.934
Not only do you have one
project.

00:01:55.934 --> 00:01:57.968
You have two giant projects
that we can talk about.

00:01:57.968 --> 00:01:59.767
So, I'm happy that you're here.

00:01:59.767 --> 00:02:02.467
I want to talk about "Super
Pumped" the story of Uber.

00:02:02.467 --> 00:02:06.934
But I want to know first about
the other show on Apple TV.

00:02:06.934 --> 00:02:08.634
This is "Suspicion."
-Yes, "Suspicion."

00:02:08.634 --> 00:02:11.100
You said it for suspiciously,
like you weren't quite sure.

00:02:11.100 --> 00:02:13.434
-No -- I'm suspicious, yeah.

00:02:13.434 --> 00:02:15.033
I don't want to give
anything away. yeah.

00:02:15.033 --> 00:02:18.400
-Don't tell anyone.
-What is "Suspicion" about?

00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:22.200
-"Suspicion" is about --
it's kind of a who done it,

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:24.701
and kind of eco-terrorism.

00:02:24.701 --> 00:02:28.334
Where sort of the good guys and
the bad guys get all mixed up.

00:02:28.334 --> 00:02:30.701
I play a cold, strong
business woman

00:02:30.701 --> 00:02:32.701
whose son has been kidnapped.
-Yeah.

00:02:32.701 --> 00:02:34.934
-Yes.
-Did you film this one

00:02:34.934 --> 00:02:36.534
during the pandemic?
-I did.

00:02:36.534 --> 00:02:39.234
I did both during the pandemic.

00:02:39.234 --> 00:02:41.934
But there were two flavors
of the joyful pandemic.

00:02:41.934 --> 00:02:45.567
There was
the pre-vaccination flavor,

00:02:45.567 --> 00:02:48.267
which "Suspicion"
was shot during.

00:02:48.267 --> 00:02:50.300
Which was really required
a lot of courage.

00:02:50.300 --> 00:02:53.434
And I think it's very important
to actually try to get back

00:02:53.434 --> 00:02:56.801
and be in the workplace.
I admit it was scary.

00:02:56.801 --> 00:02:59.100
-Yeah. We need it.
-I, in fact, did burst

00:02:59.100 --> 00:03:03.000
into my tears
in my trailer at least once.

00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:05.033
You know, when you find out
somebody maybe

00:03:05.033 --> 00:03:07.067
isn't feeling well --
-Yeah, it's scary.

00:03:07.067 --> 00:03:08.501
-It's real.
-Yeah.

00:03:08.501 --> 00:03:11.901
-And then the post-vaccination
working situation,

00:03:11.901 --> 00:03:15.467
which is a lot more cool.
-Yeah.

00:03:15.467 --> 00:03:17.767
-Yeah, a lot more fun.
-A lot more relaxed, yeah.

00:03:17.767 --> 00:03:19.467
Everyone's tested
and everyone's safe.

00:03:19.467 --> 00:03:23.767
-People test, people, you know,
like, everybody --

00:03:23.767 --> 00:03:26.701
our world is slowly, slowly,
slowly bouncing back.

00:03:26.701 --> 00:03:29.033
-Yeah, it is. Yeah, we're coming
back, absolutely, yeah.

00:03:29.033 --> 00:03:32.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:32.300 --> 00:03:34.567
"Super Pumped:
The Battle for Uber."

00:03:34.567 --> 00:03:36.501
-Yes.
-I remember --

00:03:36.501 --> 00:03:38.801
the cast is amazing, by the way.
Joseph Gordon-Levitt. Shout out.

00:03:38.801 --> 00:03:40.701
We love him. He's --
-Shout out!

00:03:40.701 --> 00:03:42.367
-Yes, I'm giving him
a shout out.

00:03:42.367 --> 00:03:45.200
[ Cheers and applause ]
Go Joe!

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:46.501
Well, you play
Arianna Huffington.

00:03:46.501 --> 00:03:49.400
-I do.
-And I -- you know her, right?

00:03:49.400 --> 00:03:52.067
-I have met her a bunch of
times. I don't know her well.

00:03:52.067 --> 00:03:53.934
-No.
-But I like her.

00:03:53.934 --> 00:03:56.501
-Yeah.
-And I try to play her.

00:03:56.501 --> 00:03:57.767
It was the best I could.
-You did a great job.

00:03:57.767 --> 00:04:00.501
Is it intimidating to play
someone that's around

00:04:00.501 --> 00:04:02.367
and can see you?
-Yeah, no,

00:04:02.367 --> 00:04:03.801
it totally is intimidating.

00:04:03.801 --> 00:04:05.567
And you do feel quite
responsible.

00:04:05.567 --> 00:04:08.267
But I kind of knew
I wouldn't get it right.

00:04:08.267 --> 00:04:10.501
I just have to, like,
put my whole heart in it

00:04:10.501 --> 00:04:12.767
and practice a lot.
-Yeah.

00:04:12.767 --> 00:04:14.534
I want to talk about
nailing the voice.

00:04:14.534 --> 00:04:15.634
I want to show a clip
when we come back.

00:04:15.634 --> 00:04:16.634
More with Uma Thurman.

